    "text": "Skip to courses\nr\nRecallWeave\nCourse catalog\n\nEXPLORE A NEW CONNECTION\n\nA small lesson.\nA new way to think.\n\nChoose a subject, see the ideas it connects, and take a course into the RecallWeave learner.\n\n4 supplied courses · Ready to use offline\n\nFrom a course to a lesson\nDownload a course JSON file below.\nOpen the learner and choose the file under Bring your own lesson.\nInspect the preview, then choose Start this deck.\nOpen learner\n↗\nin a new tab\n\nThe catalog opens the learner in a separate tab. Your current lesson stays where it is.\n\nFIND YOUR NEXT LESSON\n\nBrowse the courses\nSearch titles and concepts\n\n4 courses available.\n\n12 questions · 4 concepts\n\nBinary search: precise boundaries\nSorted search contract\nInterval decisions\nBoundary results\nProgress and cost\nA look at the questions\nSource and permissions\nDownload course (.json)\nbinary-search.json\n\nDownload requested: binary-search.json. Choose it in the learner.\n\n12 questions · 4 concepts\n\nDirected graphs: from arrows to dependency plans\ndirected-links\nreachability\ndependency-orders\ncycles-and-updates\nA look at the questions\nSource and permissions\nDownload course (.json)\ndependency-graphs.json\n\n12 questions · 4 concepts\n\nMeasurement uncertainty: what more readings can tell you\nReadings and correction\nScatter and mean\nShared calibration\nCombining and deciding\nA look at the questions\nSource and permissions\nDownload course (.json)\nmeasurement-uncertainty.json\n\n12 questions · 4 concepts\n\nSQL query foundations — rows, NULLs, groups, and joins\nrows\nnulls\ngroups\njoins\nA look at the questions\nSource and permissions\nDownload course (.json)\nsql-query-foundations.json\n\nEach download is the supplied course file, with its original source and permission statements. Open a course’s details to read them.\n\nCourses and learning sessions run locally. RecallWeave’s model estimates are illustrative; they are not grades or evidence of learning efficacy.\n\nHave a lesson to share? Open Deck studio \nin a new tab\n↗"
